    <item>
      <title>How a Gemma model helped discover a new potential cancer therapy pathway</title>
      <link>https://blog.google/technology/ai/google-gemma-ai-cancer-therapy-discovery/</link>
      <description>&lt;div style="border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; margin: 8px 0; background-color: #f9f9f9;"&gt;
&lt;div style="font-weight: bold; color: #2c3e50; margin-bottom: 8px;"&gt;
📄 Source: Google DeepMind Blog
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="font-size: 0.9em; margin-bottom: 8px;"&gt;
&lt;span style="color: #7f8c8d;"&gt;👤 Author: Google AI Team&lt;/span&gt; | &lt;span style="color: #7f8c8d;"&gt;📅 Date: 2024-04-24&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin-bottom: 8px;"&gt;
&lt;span style="background-color: #3498db; color: white; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.8em;"&gt;Artificial Intelligence&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="background-color: #3498db; color: white; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.8em;"&gt;Cancer Research&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="background-color: #3498db; color: white; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.8em;"&gt;Single-Cell Analysis&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="line-height: 1.6;"&gt;
Google AI developed Gemma, a 27 billion parameter foundation model for single-cell RNA sequencing analysis, which helped identify a novel cancer therapy pathway. This AI-driven approach enhances understanding of complex biological data, offering new opportunities for drug development and personalized medicine. Gemma is also applicable to other biomedical fields and is being made openly available to accelerate research collaborations.
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
